{
	"title": "Multiplier une fraction par un entier en simplifiant d'abord",
	"description": "Produit d'une fraction par un multiple de son dénominateur, en simplifiant d'abord (5/6 × 12 = 5 × 2 = 10)",
	"grades": ["6"],
	"theme": "Fractions",
	"domain": "Calculer",
	"subdomain": "Multiplication",
	"level": 8,
	"delay": 30,
	"status": "draft",
	"variations": [
		{
			"statement": "Calcule.\n\n$$\\frac{{{a}}}{{{b}}} \\times {{n}} = ?$$",
			"variables": [
				{
					"name": "b",
					"expression": "2..9"
				},
				{
					"name": "a",
					"expression": "1..9"
				},
				{
					"name": "k",
					"expression": "2..5"
				},
				{
					"name": "n",
					"expression": "eval:b*k"
				}
			],
			"conditions": ["gcd(a,b)==1", "a!=b"],
			"blanks": [
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "{{eval:a*k}}"
				}
			],
			"correction": {
				"steps": [
					"**Simplifier d'abord.** ${{n}}$ est un multiple de ${{b}}$ : ${{n}} = {{b}} \\times {{k}}$. On divise ${{n}}$ par ${{b}}$, puis on multiplie par ${{a}}$.",
					"$$\\frac{{{a}}}{{{b}}} \\times {{n}} = {{a}} \\times \\frac{{{n}}}{{{b}}} = {{a}} \\times {{k}} = \\textcolor{{{color:primary.0}}}{{{solution}}}$$",
					"On peut aussi multiplier d'abord : $\\frac{{{a}}}{{{b}}} \\times {{n}} = \\frac{{{a}} \\times {{n}}}{{{b}}} = \\frac{{{eval:a*n}}}{{{b}}} = {{solution}}$."
				]
			}
		}
	],
	"testSpecs": [
		{
			"description": "5/6 × 12 = 10",
			"variationIndex": 0,
			"variables": {
				"b": "6",
				"a": "5",
				"k": "2",
				"n": "12"
			},
			"answers": ["10"],
			"expected": {
				"status": "correct"
			}
		},
		{
			"description": "60/6 non simplifié : ambre",
			"variationIndex": 0,
			"variables": {
				"b": "6",
				"a": "5",
				"k": "2",
				"n": "12"
			},
			"answers": ["\\frac{60}{6}"],
			"expected": {
				"status": "unoptimal_form",
				"constraintViolations": ["reducedFractions"]
			}
		},
		{
			"description": "Erreur : 60/72",
			"variationIndex": 0,
			"variables": {
				"b": "6",
				"a": "5",
				"k": "2",
				"n": "12"
			},
			"answers": ["\\frac{60}{72}"],
			"expected": {
				"status": "incorrect"
			}
		}
	]
}
